## EF Core ##
efbundle*

## Data Protection key ring (Development default path — Production points elsewhere via
## DataProtection:KeysPath). These are secrets: they decrypt auth cookies and Identity tokens. ##
**/App_Data/

## Uploaded seminar media (Development default path — Production points elsewhere via
## Media:RootPath). Real customer-facing content, sometimes large video; it belongs on the server
## and in backups, never in the repository. ##
**/App_Media/

## Site photography. The binaries are fetched, not committed — ClientApp/media-manifest.json is the
## committed source of truth and `npm run fetch:media` reproduces this folder. Must be run before
## `dotnet publish` on a clean checkout, or every cover falls back to the crest placeholder. ##
## wwwroot/brand/ and wwwroot/video/ are NOT in the manifest and ARE committed: MapStaticAssets only
## serves files present at build time, so a CI publish without them ships a broken Coming Soon page. ##
**/wwwroot/img/
**/wwwroot/brand/*.**
**/wwwroot/video/*.**

## Node / npm / Vite (src/VIHouse.WebUI/ClientApp) ##
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.vite/

## Vite build output (regenerated by the ViteBuild MSBuild target on every `dotnet build`) ##
**/wwwroot/dist/

# Note: wwwroot/lib/ (jQuery/jquery-validation) stays tracked — it's vendored manually, not
# restored by any build step (no libman.json), so untracking it would break a fresh clone.

